@style(../styles/IDocDemo.style)
@title(Octo 20: every @@octo argument)

The arguments change how a block looks, when it runs and how long it may take. Each block below shows one.

`@@settings(module=octo, ...)` sets the run policy for every block in the document; this one runs blocks as they scroll into view and allows up to 20 seconds.

@settings(module=octo, run=visible, maxrun=20)

@section(Layout)

`output=` puts the results below, right, above or left of the code.

@octo(output=right)
x = 1:5;
plot(x, x.^2); title("output on the right");
@end

@octo(output=above)
disp("results above the code")
@end

`height=` (or `h=`) and `width=` (or `w=`), with `minwidth=`/`maxwidth=` (`minw=`/`maxw=`), size the block.

@octo(height=300, width=90%, minwidth=320, maxwidth=900)
plot(randn(1, 50)); title("sized block");
@end

@octo(h=240, w=70%, minw=300, maxw=700)
disp("short names for the same sizes")
@end

`fs=` sets the code's text size in points; `size=` takes a size word: small, large or huge.

@octo(fs=12, size=large)
disp("larger code text")
@end

Margins and spacing: `m=`, `mt=`, `mb=`, `ml=`, `mr=`, `pad=` and `gap=`; `align=` places the block.

@octo(mt=12pt, mb=12pt, ml=0, mr=0, pad=8px, gap=6px, align=center)
disp("spaced and centred")
@end

@octo(m=6pt)
disp("one margin on every side")
@end

`x=`, `y=` and `z=` position a block on a slide or a fixed page, as for other floating blocks.

@octo(x=0, y=0, z=1)
disp("positioned")
@end

@section(Looks)

`theme=` picks dark, studio or showcase; `stage=theme` makes the figure stage take the document theme's colours; `bg=` and `color=` set the background and text colour.

@octo(theme=dark)
disp("dark theme")
@end

@octo(theme=studio, stage=theme)
plot(sin(0:0.1:6)); title("stage takes the theme");
@end

@octo(theme=showcase, bg=#f4f1ea, color=#222222)
disp("showcase with custom colours")
@end

`noedit` hides the code and keeps the results.

@octo(noedit)
t = linspace(-20, 20, 400);
plot(t, sin(t) ./ t); title("sinc, code hidden");
@end

@section(When it runs and for how long)

`run=click` waits for the Run button and `run=visible` runs when scrolled into view. `limit=` gives a block more seconds; `nolim` removes the limit.

@octo(run=click, limit=10)
s = 0;
for k = 1:2e5
  s = s + 1/k^2;
end
disp(s)
@end

@octo(run=visible)
disp("ran when scrolled into view")
@end

@octo(nolim)
disp(sum(1:1e6))
@end

`benchmark=` names a timer that receives the block's run time in milliseconds; a @@benchmark block times everything inside it.

@benchmark(octo_total)
@octo(benchmark=matmul)
A = rand(200);
B = A * A;
disp(size(B))
@end
@end

@section(Grading arguments)

`id=`, `pts=` (or `points=`), `expect=`, `tolerance=` and `time=` make a question; see the grading file for each in use.

@octo(id=args1, points=1, expect="6")
disp(1 + 2 + 3)
@end
